# Re-include this directory's TypeScript sources.
#
# The repository root .gitignore has a bare `lib/` rule, which exists for Python
# packaging output and swallows this CDK app's entire source directory. Without
# this negation the committed templates would have no source to regenerate them
# and the drift gate in scripts/synth-templates.sh would be unrunnable.
#
# `!lib/` has to un-exclude the DIRECTORY, not just the files: git will not
# re-include a path whose parent directory is excluded, because it never walks
# into it. The compiled-output rules below still apply inside it, so only the
# .ts sources land.
!lib/

# CDK build and synth artifacts. tsc has no outDir, so compiled output lands
# beside each source file. The committed templates under templates/ are the
# deliverable; cdk.out is the scratch assembly that produces them.
*.js
!jest.config.js
*.d.ts
node_modules
cdk.out
dist
.cdk.staging
*.tsbuildinfo

# Test/coverage output. ash-typescript-ci.yml runs jest with --coverage here and
# uploads this directory as an artifact, so running the documented command
# locally produces it too. The sibling deploy/cdk-constructs/.gitignore already
# covers this; without the rule here the run leaves an untracked coverage/
# behind, which is easy to sweep into an unrelated commit.
coverage/
